Article 2 (Establishment and Operation of the Social Security Administrative Data Analysis Center)
(1) The Minister of Health and Welfare shall establish a social security administrative data analysis center under Article 43 (1) of the Framework Act on Social Security (hereinafter referred to as the "Act" and, in this Article, as the "Administrative Data Analysis Center") within the secretariat of the Social Security Committee under Article 21 (8) of the Act.
(2) The Administrative Data Analysis Center shall perform the following duties:
1. Preservation and management of social security administrative data;
2. Interlinking and analysis of social security administrative data;
3. Research on social security systems using social security administrative data;
4. Other duties that the Minister of Health and Welfare deems necessary for the smooth analysis, utilization, etc. of social security administrative data.
(3) The Administrative Data Analysis Center shall be equipped with security facilities that can control access, computer equipment for analysis of social security administrative data, and other necessary equipment.
(4) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (3), the Minister of Health and Welfare shall prescribe the details necessary for the establishment and operation of the Administrative Data Analysis Center.
